<name>Speaker Assembly Front NO.1</name>
<para id="RM000002BZL001X" category="G" type-id="3001K" name-id="641JS-00" from="200612">
<name>Component Inspection</name>
<subpara id="RM000002BZL001X_01" type-id="01" category="01">
<s-1 id="RM000002BZL001X_01_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000018B00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Speaker Assembly Front NO.1</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Check that the speaker installation is not loose or rattling.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check that there is no foreign matter inside the speaker and that the speaker cone paper is not torn.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Resistance Measurement</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E122035J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<s3>
<ptxt>Disconnect the front speaker assembly NO.1 connector.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Perform the measurement without removing the speaker.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the speaker terminals.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
